  "description": "The reference case for the delta projection, and for all three member-identity forms an address can carry. Retiming a runnable's timing event is a `remove` plus a `create` — the event's identity IS its value, so there is nothing inside it to update — while a field of a `field`-identified list member and an entry of a map are ordinary `update`s. The `set_*`-style tools each needed a parameter for one of these; none of them could express the first.",
